\section*{Pointwise triple ergodic averages with distinct integer slopes under mixing}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Triple averages with any three distinct nonzero integer slopes, including negative ones, are claimed to converge almost everywhere to the product of integrals for mixing transformations. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 154, 2026-10-04): The local progression estimates are extended using an integer left inverse of the complete primitive configuration. Vandermonde cancellation and a height base divisible by every slope difference preserve the Fourier and divisibility bounds through discretization, giving the slope-dependent oscillation estimate needed for convergence.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 154, 2026-10-04): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
